{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Which they made in Haran.</b> That they brought them under the wings of the Shechinah — Abraham converting the men and Sarah converting the women — and Scripture accounts it to them as though they made them. And its plain sense: slaves and maidservants that they acquired for themselves, as in ״עָשָׂה אֶת כָּל הַכָּבֹד הַזֶּה״ (ibid. 31), and ״יִשְׂרָאֵל עֹשֶׂה חָיִל״ (Numbers 24:18) — a term of acquiring and gathering."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:22.341081285Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}